From a65490eb9e3fa12a29f2e43b08238718c0cc9474 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Glozar <tglozar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 21:49:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 504/634] IA64: Migrate fsys_gettimeofday to the generic VDSO
 time data

Commit bf8f968a6315 ("vdso/vsyscall: Gate update_vsyscall() behind
CONFIG_GENERIC_GETTIMEOFDAY") and commit 96942092d5e6 ("vdso/treewide:
Drop GENERIC_TIME_VSYSCALL") removed CONFIG_GENERIC_TIME_VSYSCALL, the
hook ia64 used to provide its own update_vsyscall()/update_vsyscall_tz()
backing fsys_gettimeofday's fsyscall_gtod_data. Only architectures
selecting CONFIG_GENERIC_GETTIMEOFDAY still get real implementations;
everyone else now gets silent no-op stubs, which broke the build and
would have left fsys_gettimeofday serving stale data.

Move ia64 onto the generic VDSO time data (struct vdso_time_data)
used by kernel/time/vsyscall.c instead:

 - select HAVE_GENERIC_VDSO/GENERIC_GETTIMEOFDAY, drop
   GENERIC_TIME_VSYSCALL/ARCH_CLOCKSOURCE_DATA
 - add asm/vdso/{clocksource,processor,vsyscall}.h, with a new
   VDSO_CLOCKMODE_MMIO alongside VDSO_CLOCKMODE_ITC to keep the MMIO
   clocksource (Cyclone, HPET) fast path fsys_gettimeofday previously
   had via clocksource archdata; replace that archdata field with a
   single ia64_fsys_mmio pointer written by cyclone.c/hpet.c
 - rework fsys_gettimeofday to read vdso_k_time_data and dispatch on
   the current clock_mode (ITC, MMIO, or fall back to the real
   syscall for anything else), instead of the removed
   fsyscall_gtod_data
 - regenerate the IA64_VDSO_* asm-offsets used by fsys.S from
   struct vdso_time_data/vdso_timestamp

This is a combination of generic (VDSO) and IA-64 (fsyscall) features.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-4-5
Signed-off-by: Tomas Glozar <tglozar@gmail.com>
